.TH TCL 1 "FUZIX" "Ripple"
.SH NAME
tcl \- run the Picol Tcl subset
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tcl [-c script | file [arguments ...]]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a script, evaluate -c text, or enter an interactive Tcl-style prompt.
The command names picol, tcl and tclsh select the same interpreter.
.PP
Supported facilities include variables, procedures, lists, expr, if, while,
for, foreach, catch, source, file channels and exec. This is a small Picol
based subset, not the full Tcl language or package ecosystem.
.PP
open filename a appends to a text file. Read it later with cat filename.
exec runs a command with literal arguments and captures its standard output.
Ctrl-C interrupts and returns to the shell; exit leaves the interpreter.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
tcl /hello.tcl Ripple
cat /tcl-visits
tcl -c 'puts [expr {6 * 7}]'
.fi
